            "content": [
              {
                "type": "output_text",
                "text": "As of **today (Friday, July 31, 2026)**, the most notable “Azure AI” news is concentrated around (1) Microsoft’s latest earnings + Azure growth narrative, and (2) recent Azure AI infrastructure and “agent platform” updates.\n\n## 1) Azure growth driven by AI (earnings week)\n- Microsoft’s FY2026 Q4 results (quarter ended **June 30, 2026**) emphasized “Cloud and AI strength,” with Azure growth attributed in part to AI workloads. ([news.microsoft.com](https://news.microsoft.com/source/2026/07/29/microsoft-cloud-and-ai-strength-fuels-fourth-quarter-results-4/))  \n- Multiple write-ups this week highlight Azure reaching/clearing **$100B annual revenue** and frame it as an “AI bet paying off” (with the usual caveat of heavy AI capex). ([thenextweb.com](https://thenextweb.com/news/microsoft-q4-fy2026-azure-100-billion-ai-spending))\n\n## 2) Azure AI + HPC infrastructure expansion (recent official announcement)\n- On **July 20, 2026**, Microsoft announced it’s expanding **Azure AI and HPC infrastructure with AMD**, positioning it as part of scaling for new model and **agent-driven** workloads. ([blogs.microsoft.com](https://blogs.microsoft.com/blog/2026/07/20/microsoft-expands-azure-ai-and-hpc-infrastructure-with-amd/))\n\n## 3) “Agentic apps” + Microsoft Foundry (Build 2026 + ongoing)\n- Microsoft Build 2026 messaging strongly centers on building and running AI agents “at scale,” with **Microsoft Foundry** presented as a key platform layer for agent lifecycle management and deployment. ([news.microsoft.com](https://news.microsoft.com/build-2026/))  \n- Microsoft continues to position Foundry (surfaced at **ai.azure.com**) as an enterprise platform to “build, ground, and govern” AI apps/agents. ([ai.azure.com](https://ai.azure.com/))\n\n## 4) The fastest way to see “today’s” concrete Azure changes\nIf you mean *service-change news* (GA/preview/notices) rather than press/announcements, the most up-to-date stream is:\n- **Azure Updates** (official rollup) ([azure.microsoft.com](https://azure.microsoft.com/en-us/updates/))  \n- A convenient consolidated feed that mirrors official sources also shows many of the latest dated items (e.g., updates posted **July 30, 2026 UTC**) ([azurecharts.com](https://azurecharts.com/updates))\n\nIf you tell me what you mean by “Azure AI” (e.g., **Foundry/Azure OpenAI**, **AI Search**, **Vision/Speech**, **Copilot Studio**, **infrastructure/GPUs**), I can filter today’s items down to only the relevant announcements/updates.",
